$DIR/test.p:3:9: complex numbers are not permitted in Plutonium (they are rarely useful in systems code; use a struct of two floats)
    Plutonium has no complex number types (complex64 and complex128) and no
    complex, real or imag builtins.
    Use a struct of two floats for the real and imaginary parts.
    Complex numbers are rarely useful in systems code, and leaving them out
    keeps the code generator small.
    Use a struct:
        type Complex struct{ Re, Im float64 }
    (see "Numeric types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.2)
    (run "pluto explain E2006" for a longer explanation)
